8. ADVANCED VPC PEERING SCENARIOS
==============================================================================

8.1 Cross-Region Peering:
  - Same CIDR blocks NOT allowed (can use 10.0.0.0/16 and 172.16.0.0/16)
  - Transitive peering still NOT supported
  - Higher latency vs same-region
  - Data transfer charges apply

8.2 Multi-VPC Architecture (Hub-and-Spoke):
  ┌─────────────┐
  │   VPC-HUB   │
  └──────┬──────┘
         │
     ┌───┴────────┬────────────┐
     │            │            │
  ┌──▼──┐     ┌──▼──┐     ┌──▼──┐
  │ A   │     │ B   │     │ C   │
  └─────┘     └─────┘     └─────┘
  
  All spokes peer with hub only

8.3 VPC Mesh (Fully Connected):
  Use Transit Gateway for multiple VPCs
  - Simplifies management
  - Supports transitive routing

8.4 Network ACLs in Peering:
  Inbound Rule:  Allow traffic from peer CIDR
  Outbound Rule: Allow traffic to peer CIDR
  Remember: NACLs are stateless!

