9. COMMON PEERING ISSUES & TROUBLESHOOTING
==============================================================================

Issue 1: Peering Connection Status = "Inactive"
  → Check if both VPCs exist
  → Verify CIDR blocks don't overlap
  → Check IAM permissions

Issue 2: Ping fails between instances
  → Verify peering connection is "Active"
  → Check route tables (must have peer CIDR route)
  → Verify Security Groups allow ICMP
  → Check Network ACLs (inbound/outbound rules)

Issue 3: DNS Resolution fails
  → Enable DNS hostnames in both VPCs
  → Enable DNS support in both VPCs
  → Use private IP addresses

Issue 4: Asymmetric Routing
  → Verify route tables in BOTH VPCs
  → Ensure peering connection in both directions
  → Check for conflicting routes

Debugging Commands:
$ aws ec2 describe-vpc-peering-connections
$ aws ec2 describe-route-tables --filters Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxxxx
$ aws ec2 describe-security-groups --filters Name=vpc-id,Values=vpc-xxxxx
$ ping -c 4 <target-ip>
$ traceroute <target-ip>

